        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ગ્રંથ (granth) is a tatsama, Sanskrit grantha, \"a knot\", and then \"a book\", once leaves tied together (CDIAL 4350). It is a large or important book."
